@page "/portal/help"
@layout paa_frontend.Client.Layout.StudentPortalLayout
<div class="help-page"><h1>Student help centre</h1><p class="lead">A simple guide to checking your school information and using your portal.</p>
<section><h2>Results and report cards</h2><p>Open <b>Results</b> to choose a term and year. The official report card is the school-approved version. Use <b>Analytics</b> to compare terms, view subject performance, and open individual tests and exams.</p><p>If a report is not visible, it may not have been released yet. Try refreshing later or speak to the school office.</p></section>
<section><h2>Attendance</h2><p>Use Attendance to review the days you were present or absent. If something looks incorrect, tell your class teacher or office rather than creating a second record.</p></section>
<section><h2>Fees and transactions</h2><p>Finance shows your account activity and payment history. Keep your receipt or reference number when making a payment. Contact the bursar if a payment is missing or assigned to the wrong account.</p></section>
<section><h2>Your profile</h2><p>Check that your name, class, contact details, and other personal information are correct. Ask the office to change information you cannot edit yourself.</p></section>
<section><h2>Good to know</h2><p>Sign out on shared devices. If a page stays blank, refresh once, check your connection, and report the page name and what you were trying to do.</p></section></div>
<style>.help-page{max-width:900px;margin:32px auto;padding:0 20px;color:#0f172a}.help-page h1{font-size:32px;margin:0 0 8px}.lead{color:#64748b;margin-bottom:26px}.help-page section{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:18px;padding:20px;margin:14px 0;box-shadow:0 4px 14px #0f172a0a}.help-page h2{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 8px}.help-page p{line-height:1.65;color:#475569}</style>
